{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('plan-recovery-adopts.json'))\np['description']=\\\"Discriminator: with the recovering replica holding only a default record for (1,0) and a peer reporting the instance COMMITTED at vbal 0, does the recovery adopt the committed vector, and if it does not, what vector does it end up committing? The harness drives the whole recovery path in order: the Prepare/PrepareReply resolution, the phase-1 restart the resolution starts, that restart's PreAccept/PreAcceptReply round, and the Accept/AcceptReply round it causes, reading accept count and record status only from the record currently in InstanceSpace. Prefix: the peer's record is prepared as COMMITTED with a real PUT command and the recovering replica's record is a default NONE record; all messages travel through the real Marshal/Unmarshal form. Controls: the harness prints which message codes each step produced, so an unreached round is visible rather than silent.\\\"\np['harness']['semantic_changes'][0]=\\\"harness-only scaffolding: two Replica values are constructed in-package instead of through New(), per-peer buffers replace the TCP transport, and the recovery is entered directly through startRecoveryForInstance instead of the execution timeout; all protocol messages still travel through the real Marshal/Unmarshal form and all decisions are made by the unmodified handlers\\\"\np['harness']['semantic_changes'].append(\\\"the harness drives the queued rounds explicitly and in order (PreAccept, its reply, Accept, its reply) and re-reads InstanceSpace after every delivery, because startPhase1 replaces the record object\\\")\np['monitors']=[m for m in p['monitors'] if m['id']=='M1-recovery-resolution']\np['monitors'].append({\\\"id\\\":\\\"M2-recovery-outcome\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH2-recovery-outcome\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"recovery_outcome\\\",\n \\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB2-prepare-resolution\\\"],\n \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\",\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB2-prepare-resolution\\\"],\n  \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The outcome event is read after the whole recovery path has been driven, so it reports the vector the recoverer actually committed and the vector the peer already had for the same instance.\\\",\n  \\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The recovery ran for the same instance and completed the rounds it started.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"instance\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"committed_reply.instance\\\"}],\n \\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"committed_reply\\\"})\np['observable_properties']=[q for q in p['observable_properties'] if q['checker_id']=='CH1-recovery-adopts-committed']\np['observable_properties'].append({\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH2-recovery-outcome\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\n \\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"recovery_outcome\\\"},\n \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"vectors_match\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n \\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"instance\\\"],\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"If the recovering replica ends up committing the instance, the command it commits must be the command the replica that already committed the same instance holds.\\\"})\np['uncertainties']=[\\\"The harness prepares the peer's COMMITTED record directly; a full history is not constructed.\\\",\\\"The outcome is observed for one instance and one recovery attempt; later Commit propagation to other replicas is not driven.\\\"]\njson.dump(p,open('plan-recovery-outcome.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Corrected observation for the same unit and obligation, replacing the artifact whose accept-round property was shown to observe the wrong round. The harness now drives every queued round explicitly and re-reads the record after each delivery, so the accept count and the final status come from the record currently in InstanceSpace; the plan keeps the reviewed adoption property and replaces the unreached accept-round property with an outcome property that compares the vector the recoverer commits with the vector the already-committed replica holds. The local construction run shows the recoverer reaching COMMITTED with a NOOP command while the peer holds a PUT, i.e. two different committed vectors for one instance, but the formal observation is left to the trusted runner.\\\",\n \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"unit-C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-recovery-outcome.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_recvbal_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{}}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-check3.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-check3.json 2>&1 | head -12\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
